{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124211","id":4754259433,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG2A96Q","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124211","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124211.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124211.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124211","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124211/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124211/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124211/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/c4cf3f152a008dc62fc6440e725375980de566a6","number":124211,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add support for `gl_ClipDistance`","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Still very early WIP.\r\n\r\nThis PR add support for `gl_ClipDistance` to shaders so we can selectively create a clipping volume.\r\n\r\nRight now this PR adds the shader variabes `CLIP_DISTANCE0` through `CLIP_DISTANCE5` to create up to 6 clipping calculations. For now I chose to make this shader logic instead of some sort of global implementation to prevent introducing many shader variations, but this does make it a slighly more user unfriendly to use.\r\n\r\nGLSL also has support for `gl_CullDistance`, the difference here is that while `gl_ClipDistance` discard fragments, cull distance discards entire polygons that are outside of the clipping volume. \r\n\r\nThe screenshot below shows this used to create a cylinder clipping volume. \r\n<img width=\"1358\" height=\"939\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/04e33a00-75a2-4c4d-90b4-8e713b523438\" />\r\n\r\nTest project: https://codeberg.org/BastiaanOlij/test-clip-distance\r\n\r\nPossible things that need to be investigated further:\r\n- [ ] Should we expose cull distance or do something behind the scenes to set both clip distance and cull distance?\r\n- [ ] `gl_ClipDistance` and `gl_CullDistance` seem to have core Vulkan support, but we may need to check the maximum number of clipping values\r\n- [ ] OpenGL support may require the inclusion of an OpenGL extension, if not supported, we need to have some clear way to deal with this\r\n- [ ] Needs to be checked against metal and dx12 support\r\n- [ ] Right now we're relying on automatic detection of how many clipping planes are used. May need to tighten this up\r\n- [ ] This does not impact frustum culling, objects entirely outside of the culling volume will still be attempted to render, need to look into solutions for that\r\n- [ ] Would be nice if we can properly support `float[]` instead of the hardcoded 0..5 values.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description"